# API answers

How every coordinator route answers: a JSON body with the status it means. A
refusal is the same small document everywhere, so a worker reads one shape for
every way a request can fail:

```text
{"error": "stale_lease", "detail": "the lease on u-17 moved on", "retryable": false}
```

`error` is a stable code a program branches on; `detail` is for the person
reading the log; `retryable` says whether the same request may succeed later
unchanged (a database that is down) or never will (a malformed body).

## Note
A JSON answer with a status.

## To answerJson (status: Int, body: Text) -> Response:
    Let mutable r be json(body).
    Set r's status to status.
    Return r.

## Note
The refusal document.

## To errorBody (code: Text, detail: Text, retryable: Bool) -> Text:
    Let mutable flag be "false".
    If retryable:
        Set flag to "true".
    Return "{{\"error\":" + jsonQuote(code) + ",\"detail\":" + jsonQuote(detail) + ",\"retryable\":" + flag + "}}".

## Note
A refusal of a request that will never succeed as sent.

## To refuse (status: Int, code: Text, detail: Text) -> Response:
    Return answerJson(status, errorBody(code, detail, false)).

## Note
A request the coordinator could not serve right now — its database is
unreachable or busy. The same request may succeed in a moment.

## To unavailable (detail: Text) -> Response:
    Return answerJson(503, errorBody("unavailable", detail, true)).

## Note
The usual refusals, by what was wrong.

## To badRequest (detail: Text) -> Response:
    Return refuse(400, "bad_request", detail).

## To tooLarge (limit: Int) -> Response:
    Return refuse(413, "too_large", "the body is larger than this route's {limit} bytes").

## To missing (what: Text) -> Response:
    Return refuse(404, "not_found", what + " is not known to the coordinator").

## Note
The status an answer gets when it is a list: an empty list is still an answer.
Only a missing subject is a 404.

## To listStatus (subjectExists: Bool) -> Int:
    If subjectExists:
        Return 200.
    Return 404.

## Test: api refusals are one JSON shape

Let r be badRequest("holder is missing").
Expect that r's status is equal to 400.
Expect that r's contentType is equal to "application/json".
Expect that r's body is equal to "{{\"error\":\"bad_request\",\"detail\":\"holder is missing\",\"retryable\":false}}".
Expect that jsonValid(r's body) is equal to true.

## Test: api outages are retryable and nothing else is

Let down be unavailable("the database did not answer").
Expect that down's status is equal to 503.
Expect that down's body contains "\"retryable\":true".
Expect that tooLarge(16)'s status is equal to 413.
Expect that tooLarge(16)'s body contains "16 bytes".
Expect that missing("problem opdp:1")'s status is equal to 404.

## Test: api details are escaped

Let r be refuse(409, "dead_end", "a \"quoted\" reason\nover two lines").
Expect that jsonValid(r's body) is equal to true.
Expect that answerJson(201, "[]")'s status is equal to 201.

## Test: api lists answer even when empty

For all booleans exists:
    Let status be listStatus(exists).
    Expect that (status is equal to 200) is equal to exists.
    Let flag be errorBody("x", "y", exists).
    Expect that jsonValid(flag) is equal to true.
